# The 25 Lean-emitted body-hash chain witnesses (`Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.MinaStateBodyHashChain`):
# ~80 MB of trace text against a repository whose largest tracked file is 10 MB. GENERATED, not
# tracked — emit them with the COMPILED exe (the interpreter costs minutes PER LINK):
#
#     cd metatheory && lake build mina_fp_chain_emit \
#       && ./.lake/build/bin/mina_fp_chain_emit ../circuit/tests/fixtures 0 25
#
# ⚑ The two counts are separate deliberately: `0 25` skips the 25 phase-1 chainlink traces this
# gate does not need. A gate that costs an extra 25 minutes of rendering before it can run at all
# is a gate every machine reports RED and everyone learns to ignore.
#
# The 25 PUBLIC-INPUT vectors ARE tracked one directory up (`../pasta-fp-bodyhash-pis.txt`) — they
# are small, and they are the object the head weld, the tail weld and the continuity claim are
# about, so §0/§1 of both gates run with no emit at all.
link-*-trace.txt
link-*-pis.txt
